From 64bc66a1077006bdd7481f3175aa3dd1b95a3819 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work10_kasan_plan <adbtrr_work10_kasan_plan@local>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:22:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mm/kasan: add the KASan runtime, ported from NuttX

Phase 1 of the KASan plan: the core runtime and its build wiring. Nothing
calls into it yet, so this commit is dormant by default and changes no
behaviour. The allocator hooks that make it live are phase 2.

Ported from Apache NuttX mm/kasan at commit b4aa94d, which is Apache-2.0
like TizenRT. The ASF headers are retained and each file records what it
was derived from.

New files:
  os/include/tinyara/mm/kasan.h  public interface, no-op when disabled
  os/mm/kasan/generic.c          shadow map
  os/mm/kasan/hook.c             __asan_* entry points the compiler calls
  os/mm/kasan/Make.defs          build rules
  os/mm/kasan/Kconfig            configuration

The shadow map holds one bit per machine word rather than the byte per
eight bytes used by Linux and by user space AddressSanitizer, costing
about 3 percent of covered RAM instead of 12.5. Measured at ARM32 word
width: 2060 bytes of shadow for a 64 KB region, or 1/31.8. It is carved
out of the tail of each region by kasan_register(), so no linker script
work is needed on any board. Checking stays off until the first region
registers, which is what lets the whole image be instrumented without
excluding the boot path.

Deliberate differences from upstream, each noted in the file that carries
it:

  - The tag modes are omitted. They need ARMv8 top byte ignore or ARMv8.5
    MTE and no TizenRT target has either. Global data checking is left for
    a later phase; it needs a two pass link and linker script support.
  - Reports go to lowsyslog() rather than lldbg(), which expands to
    nothing unless CONFIG_DEBUG, CONFIG_DEBUG_ERROR and CONFIG_ARCH_LOWPUTC
    all happen to be set. A report that prints nothing before panicking is
    worse than none.
  - dump_stack() is called only under CONFIG_FRAME_POINTER, which is the
    only configuration that declares it.
  - The region table bound, the minimum region size and the granule
    alignment of a region base are checked unconditionally rather than
    through DEBUGASSERT(), which compiles away without CONFIG_DEBUG. A
    sanitizer must not corrupt memory when its own limits are exceeded.
  - The shadow dump formats its own hex instead of calling sprintf() on a
    256 byte stack buffer, and prints ".." for bytes outside any region
    rather than dereferencing them. Upstream reads 80 bytes either side of
    the faulting address unconditionally, which can fault a second time
    while reporting on a target with no MMU.
  - kasan_is_poisoned() accounts for the offset of an access within its
    first granule. Upstream derives the granule count from the size alone,
    so an unaligned access straddling a granule boundary is checked against
    the first granule only. That blind spot sits exactly where an overflow
    leaves a block: sweeping every offset and length across a block
    boundary missed 28 detections before this change and none after. This
    and the bounds checking above are corrections rather than adaptations
    and should be offered back upstream.

Note that os/mm/Makefile compiles the whole directory with one CFLAGS, so
the -fno-sanitize=kernel-address in kasan/Make.defs excludes all of os/mm
from instrumentation, not just kasan/. That is intended and matches
upstream: the sanitizer must not instrument itself, and the free path
writes its delay list link into a block it has just poisoned.

Verified on the host, since the runtime is target independent apart from
word size:

  - Compiles clean under -Wall -Werror with the board warning set, at -O0,
    -O2 and -Os, in generic mode, in MM_KASAN_NONE mode and with KASan
    disabled, at both 64 and 32 bit word width.
  - Provides every symbol the compiler emits calls to with the flag set
    this port uses; an instrumented object links against it with nothing
    unresolved.
  - Eight functional tests pass at both word widths, covering the carve
    arithmetic, poison and unpoison, the multi word mask paths, the
    registration refusals, unregister, the start and stop gate, end to end
    detection of overflow, underflow and use after free through real
    instrumented code, and the dump at a region edge.
  - With KASan disabled every entry point compiles to nothing at the call
    site, so the phase 2 hooks will cost nothing when it is off.
